  "operator_only_note": "Every command passed its postcondition on both sites, so per the 9 blocker rule nothing becomes operator-only. Still operator-only by design: unsupported pages, a Jellyfin that is logged out, and play() rejections (Broker real click).",
  "side_effects_and_rules_for_phase_3": [
    "Do NOT write V.volume in production adapters: Jellyfin persists video volume into localStorage 'volume' and YouTube re-applies its own volume on load (the spike clamped to 0.03 and restored both afterwards).",
    "Jellyfin playback bumps PlayCount/LastPlayedDate of each played item (server-side UserData) - expected for real use; the spike restored them (S2E6 LastPlayedDate could not be reset to null through POST /UserItems/{id}/UserData).",
    "YouTube's own pauses come through navigator.mediaSession; a headset/AVRCP pause looks identical to a user pause in the page.",
    "Target windows by `window id` (stable), never by index; the user's own Safari window was never touched.",
    "YouTube enforces Trusted Types: innerHTML assignments from injected JS throw - use DOM methods (replaceChildren) in snippets."
  ],
